# CTO audit finding: Dockerfile did `COPY . .` with no .dockerignore, pulling .git history and
# local build artifacts into the build context - unnecessary build-context bloat and, in the
# build stage's own filesystem, exposure of anything that shouldn't be there even though the
# final runtime stage only copies /app/publish out of it.

## Build outputs (rebuilt fresh inside the image)
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Dd]ebugPublic/
[Rr]elease/
[Rr]eleases/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Pp]ublish/

## VCS / editor
.git
.gitignore
.vs/
.idea/

## Secrets - never let a local override with real credentials end up in the build context
appsettings.*.local.json
appsettings.Production.json
secrets.json

## Logs
*.log

## Python cache (import_autoplac_v3.py)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

## OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

## Claude/CI-local files not needed at build/runtime
.claude/
.github/
